  "rules": [
    "Apply a persistent downward bias correction of 3-5 EUR to all forecast horizons, as the model consistently overestimates prices by failing to capture the structural downtrend from the 76 EUR peak.",
    "Incorporate a 'lagged mean reversion' mechanism: when history shows a sharp drop (e.g., >2 EUR in 2 days), the model's flat or slightly rising trajectory must be overridden to project an immediate 1-2 EUR drop in the next 3-5 days.",
    "Treat positive sentiment spikes (0.33) as noise rather than drivers; the model incorrectly uses these to sustain upward forecasts, whereas true outcomes show immediate price rejection and decline.",
    "Adjust for 'overshoot after spikes' by forcing a steeper initial decline in the forecast curve immediately following any historical high, rather than the model's gradual flattening.",
    "Extend the mean reversion horizon: the model assumes a quick return to ~71 EUR, but true data shows a prolonged lower range (66-68 EUR) for 15+ days; extend the low-price plateau in forecasts."
  ]
}
